{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PRE-CUTOVER VERIFICATION IN THE PRODUCTION CONTAINER — the flip mechanism, the Anthropic baseline, and the kill-switch direction all proven BEFORE touching the service. Container compose-review-bot-1 on i-00880b2c7f13527c5, image id 864df2fbfcaf (Created 2026-08-03T22:06:37Z, built from current main). Slots supplied at 'docker compose exec' level only — the service definition was NOT modified, so nothing was cut over by this probe.\n\nSTEP 1 — CLASS-SLOT RESOLUTION WITH THE SLOTS SET (zero LLM spend). rebar's own load_class_slots()/resolve_class() inside the container:\n    REBAR_LLM_FRONTIER_MODEL = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    REBAR_LLM_STANDARD_MODEL = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    REBAR_LLM_TRIVIAL_MODEL  = bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n    REBAR_LLM_MODEL          = None\n  resolved:\n    frontier -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8\n    standard -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\n    trivial  -> bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0\n  exit 0. The additive three-slot instrument resolves exactly as the Approach predicts, in the real container, and preserves the per-pass split (frontier != standard).\n\nSTEP 2 — BASELINE RESOLUTION WITH NO SLOTS SET, i.e. what the bot does TODAY:\n    frontier -> anthropic:claude-opus-4-8\n    standard -> anthropic:claude-sonnet-4-6\n    trivial  -> anthropic:claude-haiku-4-5\n  exit 0. Two things follow, and both were previously assumed rather than shown:\n  (a) THE PRE-CUTOVER PATH IS DIRECT ANTHROPIC, evidenced from the container's own resolution rather than inferred from the absence of env vars.\n  (b) THE KILL SWITCH'S MECHANISM IS PROVEN IN THE SUBTRACTIVE DIRECTION: with the slots absent, resolution falls back to the built-in class defaults which are anthropic:claude-*. Deleting the three lines therefore restores the Anthropic path by construction, in this image. (This is the MECHANISM only — the end-to-end criterion below still requires executing the switch post-cutover and observing a real LLM-Review vote on the Anthropic path, because a working mechanism does not by itself prove the credential works.)\n\nSTEP 3 — ONE REAL BEDROCK CALL through rebar's OWN provider builder, from inside the production container, on the cheapest class:\n    build_bedrock_provider(...) -> BedrockProvider\n    BedrockConverseModel('us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0', provider=<that provider>) + Agent.run_sync\n    output: CUTOVER_PROBE_OK\n    usage:  RunUsage(input_tokens=21, output_tokens=11, requests=1)\n  exit 0. So in the production container, on the CURRENT image: the provider package resolves, the provider constructs, the ambient instance-role credential authenticates, the region resolves, and the inference profile invokes. One request, 32 tokens total.\n\nHONEST CAVEAT ON STEP 3's construction: I passed a minimal stand-in object exposing bedrock_region_name='us-east-1' rather than a fully loaded LLMConfig, because build_bedrock_provider(cfg) reads only that attribute (bedrock_model.py:67). So STEP 3 exercises the real builder, the real BedrockProvider, the real BedrockConverseModel and a real Bedrock invocation, but does NOT exercise config loading. STEP 1 covers the config/slot side separately and with rebar's real loader. Neither step is a substitute for the live gate vote required by the criteria below.\n\nWHAT THIS MEANS FOR THE ORDERING CRITERION. Item (d) — an observed successful pydantic_ai.providers.bedrock import inside the running container — is SATISFIED, and satisfied more strongly than asked: not just the import but a full live invocation. It was also satisfiable BEFORE any change, which is the opposite of the criterion's premise (see the preceding correction comment). Items (a) the runbook kill-switch entry and (b) the Bedrock client-error alarm are in the safety-net change now in review; item (c) the induced VOTER_ERROR alarm transition is the one still outstanding and is deliberately being run AFTER that change takes its votes, so the gate is not taken down underneath my own change."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785796226504568001,"uuid":"a9a4c381-feb6-46a3-ba50-ff93b2fc7103"}